title: WordPress Plugin Backdoor Beaconing to tascredit-pay.com (WP connect Supply Chain)
id: 3f2c6c1e-8d47-4bd6-9a3e-2c5c7d1b90af
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects a host contacting tascredit-pay.com, the attacker-controlled server
    used by the backdoored WP connect WordPress plugin releases distributed on
    22 November 2026 (CVE-2026-135202). Each affected build - Air WP Sync, WP
    Sync for Notion, Add-on Brevo for Gravity Forms and the Contact Form 7
    Airtable/Notion add-ons - loaded the same remote-control module, which used
    a WP-Cron event to send the site URL, PHP, WordPress and OS versions and the
    server user to that domain, then executed PHP returned in the response. The
    module also exposed shell command execution, password hash theft and
    webshell planting. WordPress.org's Protect The Shire hold stopped the builds
    before they shipped as updates, so a hit means a site obtained the
    malicious package another way or a staging copy already calls home.
references:
    - https://wordfence.com/blog/2026/11/supply-chain-compromise-backdoors-six-wp-connect-plugins-blocked-by-wordpress-orgs-release-hold
    - https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-135202
    - https://securityonline.info/wordpress-plugin-backdoor-cve-2026-135202/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/24
tags:
    - attack.t1195
    - attack.t1071
    - attack.t1100
logsource:
    category: network_connection
detection:
    selection:
        DestinationHostname|endswith: 'tascredit-pay.com'
    condition: selection
falsepositives:
    - Threat-intel research, sandbox detonation, URL scanners or analyst pivots that deliberately resolve the reported C2 domain
    - Archival copies of the malicious plugin builds (quarantine, malware sandboxes, backup snapshots) replayed in a lab network
level: critical
